ore_rev_volatility":76.7,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.3339335145339419,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.29641571608033457,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":7.067903141558826,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.4657586223724178,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.01320944563800186,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":31.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.03589510403861881,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":14.1,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03648826674473016,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":4.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.042692540933899334,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":28.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.03995,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":26.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Myriad Genetics, Inc., a molecular diagnostics and precision medicine company, develops molecular tests. It offers molecular diagnostic tests for oncology, women's health, and pharmacogenomics. It provides MyRisk Hereditary Cancer test, a DNA sequencing test for hereditary cancers; BRACAnalysis CDx Germline Companion Diagnostic test, a DNA sequencing test for metastatic breast, ovarian, metastatic pancreatic, and metastatic prostate cancer with deleterious or suspected deleterious germline BRCA variants; and MyChoice CDx Companion Diagnostic, a tumor test that determines homologous recombination deficiency status in patients with ovarian cancer. It offers Prolaris Prostate Cancer Prognostic, an RNA expression tumor analysis for assessing the aggressiveness of prostate cancer; EndoPredict Breast Cancer Prognostic, an RNA expression test for assessing the aggressiveness of breast cancer; Precise Tumor Molecular Profile, a genomic profiling test; Prequel Prenatal Screen, a prenatal screening test to screen chromosomal disorders in a fetus; Foresight Carrier Screen, a prenatal test for future parents to assess risk of passing on recessive genetic condition to offspring; SneakPeek Early Gender DNA, a non-invasive blood test that predicts the fetus's gender; FirstGene; and GeneSight Psychotropic Mental Health Medication, a DNA genotyping test to aid psychotropic drug selection for depression, anxiety, attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder, and other mental health conditions. It has a license collaboration with Illumina, Inc.; University of Texas M.D. Anderson Cancer Center; Mayo Foundation for Medical Education and Research; Children's Medical Center in Boston; Institut Curie and INSERM; and Eurobio Scientific SA. The company has a strategic alliance with SOPHiA GENETICS SA to advance new prostate cancer-specific genomic instability score technology for oncology approaches with AstraZeneca. The company was founded in 1991 and is headquartered in Salt Lake City, Utah.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Samraat S. Raha | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $305K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 5%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Myriad Genetics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $543M market cap on $824M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -19% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 70% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $14M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -36.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 47% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 68/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 173% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Myriad Genetics (NASDAQ:MYGN) Stock Gets Price Target Increase from Stephens","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/myriad-genetics-nasdaqmygn-stock-gets-price-target-increase-from-stephens.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794490983.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.681,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Shereen Solaiman Awarded 83,049 Stock Options by Myriad Genetics","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/shereen-solaiman-awarded-83049-stock-options-by-myriad-genetics","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794280302.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Myriad Genetics CFO Benjamin Wheeler Awarded 121,379 Stock Options in Retention Grant","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/myriad-genetics-cfo-benjamin-wheeler-awarded-121379-stock-options-in-retention-grant","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794280299.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Myriad Genetics COO Mark Verratti Awarded 146,933 Stock Options in November 2026 Retention Grant","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/myriad-genetics-coo-mark-verratti-awarded-146933-stock-options-in-november-2026-retention